WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:06.330
You might be already using a floater health
insurance for your family. You must have opted

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:11.190
for that, because buying floater health insurance
for the whole family is cheaper than buying

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:16.910
separate health insurance policy for each
family member. Can you do the same for your

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:22.609
Car and bike? Is it possible to buy a floater
insurance policy for your car and bike together

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:28.130
and save on insurance premium? Yes. You can
do this with motor floater policy which is

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.120
introduced now in India. In this video, I
will explain how to reduce your car insurance

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.390
costs every year using the motor floater policy.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:51.170
Welcome to Save and Invest Smartly!

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:58.830
The floater motor insurance plan is a part
of the sandbox initiative, where insurers

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:05.149
can experiment and test innovative financial
products. The sandbox approach gives an opportunity

00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:10.830
to experiment and learn about new technology
and product, before it’s finally adopted

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:16.290
and offered to larger set of people. The insurance
companies that has rolled out motor floater

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:22.500
policy are ICICI Lombard General Insurance
and Reliance General Insurance

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.610
What is motor floater policy?
It is a single insurance policy that covers

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:32.420
all the vehicles owned by a person, together.
All private vehicles, cars or two-wheelers

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.310
registered under a single owner can be covered
under this policy.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.110
Maximum of up to 5 vehicles can be covered
under the same policy.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:46.110
How is the Sum Insured calculated?
Every vehicle has an IDV - Insured Declared

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:53.040
Value, fixed by the insurer based on the brand,
model and age of the vehicle. It may be approximately

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.610
equivalent to the market value of the vehicle.
For example, let us consider you own a car,

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:04.040
a bike and a scooter all registered under
your name. If the IDV value for each of these,

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.950
arrived based on market value are let's say, Car - 500000

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:13.110
Bike - 35000,  Scooter - 15000

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:18.450
In case of motor floater policy, IDV of
each vehicle is calculated separately and

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:24.069
the one with highest IDV is the primary vehicle
and other vehicles are considered secondary

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:27.160
vehicles. In our case,
 the car becomes the Primary Vehicle

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.920
and the Bike and Scooter become the  Secondary Vehicles

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.150
The Sum Insured is the IDV of the primary
vehicle.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.040
Therefore the Sum Insured in our case
is 500000

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.920
The Sub limit of each insured vehicle depends
on individual IDV

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:45.790
For example, if the bike is lost and you
apply for claim under the floater policy,

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:50.120
then the maximum claim is limited to 35000
as per its IDV.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.970
With every claim, the sum insured of the
policy also reduces.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:59.580
For example, if you have claimed 35000 for
your bike when it is lost, the updated sum

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:05.140
insured will be (500000-35000)=465000 .

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.470
The Sum Insured will be reset to maximum value
automatically during the next year policy renewal.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:15.319
But in case, you want to reset the sum insured
mid year, then you may do it by paying an

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:17.080
additional amount.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.909
What are the Coverage Options available?
You may choose any of the 2 coverage options that are available

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:24.220
Option 1: Stand Alone Own Damage Cover

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:30.030
Own Damage Insurance&nbsp;is a customized motor&nbsp;insurance&nbsp;policy
designed to protect you and your insured vehicle

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:34.910
from your&nbsp;own damages. That is, this policy
covers against any loss or damage to your

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:39.879
vehicle or its accessories due to:&nbsp;
Fire, explosion, self-ignition, accidental

00:03:39.879 --> 00:03:42.739
damage
or during Transit, that is when the vehicle is shifted

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:46.590
from one place to another
Natural disasters like earthquake, flood,

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:50.450
cyclone, etc.
or Burglary, theft, riot, etc.,

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:55.099
Option 2: Own Damage with Third Party
This option covers everything in Option 1

00:03:55.099 --> 00:03:58.640
plus the third party coverage.
Third party policy&nbsp;covers the&nbsp;insured&nbsp;against

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:04.390
any legal liability arising out towards third
parties due to accidental injury or death

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:08.040
of a person and any damage caused to third
party property.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.780
Let's see the advantages of motor floater
policy:

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:16.720
You can buy one single floater motor insurance
plan that covers all vehicles that you own.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.630
Some of you may have 2 cars or some of you
may have a car and a bike, or some people

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:26.650
may have 2 or 3 bikes in their family. All
these could be covered using a single floater

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:31.530
motor insurance policy. This will save a lot
of time as the insurance buying or renewal

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:36.020
process would be only once a year for all
vehicles together.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:41.160
You don't have to fill up several proposal
forms and submit proofs for each vehicle separately.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.660
A single documentation is sufficient for all
the vehicles together.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:49.940
There is no hassle of remembering multiple
renewal dates. Just remember one date for

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.120
renewing the policy in a year for all vehicles
together.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.560
If you have to update some details in
your policies like change of address, etc.,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.620
you may do it in a single go for all vehicles
together.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.530
The premium paid for a floater policy
covering all vehicles together is lesser than

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.440
the total premium paid, if separate policies
are bought for each vehicle. You may save

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.410
up to 20% on your premium if you go for motor
floater policy.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:20.340
You can add or delete vehicles later easily
to the same policy, whenever you buy a new

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.160
vehicle or sell one of the existing vehicle.
All other regular motor insurance benefits

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:30.729
like no claim bonus, cancellation, etc are
also available on the motor floater policy.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:33.040
How to apply for motor floater policy?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.819
If you want to get the insurance from ICICI
Lombard General Insurance,

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:43.040
visit www.icicilombard.com. You will see
various menu options.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.159
Click on Products and then select the
option "Single Owner Multiple Vehicle".

00:05:47.159 --> 00:05:51.910
You will get a form to fill up your name,
mobile number and email id. Fill up the details

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:56.460
and tick the check box to agree the terms
and conditions. Click on Proceed.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:00.210
This will take you to the next page to
fill up the number of vehicles. From the first

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.569
drop down, select the number cars you own
and from the next drop down, select the number

00:06:04.569 --> 00:06:09.350
of two wheelers that you own. Click on 'Submit'.
The insurance agent will contact you to

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:13.110
get further details from you and proceed with
the documentation.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:16.710
To apply the motor floater policy from Reliance
General Insurance,

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:23.110
visit www.reliancegeneral.co.in. You will
see various menu options.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:27.360
Click on the menu 'Car' and then select
the option 'Motor Floater Insurance'.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.830
You will get a form to fill up your name
and contact details. Fill up the form, tick the

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.880
check box and click on 'Submit'.
The insurance agent will contact you to

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:39.759
get further details from you and proceed with
the documentation.

00:06:39.759 --> 00:06:43.690
The floater policy will definitely save time
and money for you in the long run. Give it

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:48.330
a try when you apply or renew your car insurance
or bike insurance next time. Let me know your

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:52.669
thoughts on this new policy type in the comments
section. Also, write down if you have more

00:06:52.669 --> 00:06:53.830
queries on this.

